# Event Pipeline

> **Pivot active:** New work uses the **target** flow below. Legacy flow still in codebase until pivot phases land. See `docs/DATASET_PLATFORM.md`.

## Target flow (dataset pivot)

```
project.submitted → intake.completed → preprocessing.completed → planning.completed
  → annotation.task.dispatched (×N) → annotation.task.completed (×N) → export.completed
```

Step Functions handles annotation fan-out in prod. Local: simplified sequential fan-out.

## Legacy flow (research — being removed)

```
query.submitted → ingestion.completed → embedding.completed → knowledge.mined
  → research.task.dispatched (×N) → research.task.completed (×N) → synthesis.completed
```

## Event naming

`eventforge.<domain>.<action>` — e.g. `eventforge.query.submitted`

## Required fields (every event)

`event_id`, `correlation_id`, `job_id`, `timestamp`, `schema_version`, `detail_type`, `payload`

Define JSON Schema in `shared/events/` before the producer ships. Mirror as Pydantic in `backend/src/eventforge/events/schemas/`.

**Incremental policy:** bootstrap with envelope + `query.submitted` (KRE-122); add each stage's output schema when that worker is implemented. See `shared/events/README.md`.

## Stage map (target)

| Event in                      | Worker         | Event out                    | Stores              |
| ----------------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------- |
| project.submitted             | Intake         | intake.completed             | assets → Postgres   |
| intake.completed              | Preprocessing  | preprocessing.completed    | segments → Postgres |
| preprocessing.completed       | Planning       | planning.completed           | tasks → Postgres    |
| annotation.task.dispatched    | Annotation     | annotation.task.completed  | batches → Postgres  |
| all annotation done           | Export         | export.completed             | export → Postgres   |

## Stage map (legacy)

| Event in                 | Worker    | Event out               | Stores                        |
| ------------------------ | --------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| query.submitted          | Ingestion | ingestion.completed     | sources → Postgres            |
| ingestion.completed      | Embedding | embedding.completed     | vectors → Postgres (pgvector) |
| embedding.completed      | Knowledge | knowledge.mined         | entities → Postgres           |
| research.task.dispatched | Research  | research.task.completed | notes → Postgres              |
| all research done        | Synthesis | synthesis.completed     | report → Postgres             |

## Resilience

- SQS `maxReceiveCount: 3` → `eventforge-dlq`
- Idempotency: `processed_events(event_id PK, worker_name, processed_at)`
- Terminal failure: emit `pipeline.failed`, update JobStage → `failed`, push to SSE
- LLM calls: 3 retries, exponential backoff

## Queues (LocalStack + prod)

`eventforge-intake`, `eventforge-preprocessing`, `eventforge-planning`, `eventforge-annotation`, `eventforge-export`, `eventforge-dlq`

Legacy queue names (`eventforge-ingestion`, etc.) may still exist in archived Terraform — not used by the dataset pivot.
